Package: InsectTrack
Type: Package
Title: Detection, Tracking and Activity Mapping of Insects in Videos
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8401-472X")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: Detects and tracks insects in videos and converts their
    trajectories into activity measures: counts, activity time series,
    occupancy heat maps and hot spots, visits to regions of interest such as
    flowers, insects entering and leaving nests and hives, and proximity
    interactions. One function analyses a whole video and writes an annotated
    video with a coloured trajectory and identity label for every insect,
    tables, figures and a report. Detection uses trained 'YOLO' models,
    open-vocabulary detectors driven by a text prompt ('Grounding DINO',
    'OWLv2'), or background subtraction implemented in R and C++; 'SAM 2.1'
    outlines detected insects to measure body size and to pre-label frames for
    annotation. Tracking uses optimal assignment with motion prediction, 'SORT'
    or 'ByteTrack' implemented in R, or the trackers of the Python package
    'BoxMOT'. Detections and tracks can be evaluated against annotations with
    standard multi-object tracking metrics (CLEAR MOT, IDF1, HOTA).
